  "question": {
    "text": "The solution curve, of the differential equation $2 y \\frac{\\mathrm{d} y}{\\mathrm{~d} x}+3=5 \\frac{\\mathrm{d} y}{\\mathrm{~d} x}$, passing through the point $(0,1)$ is a conic, whose vertex lies on the line:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "qnwGC",
      "text": "$2 x+3 y=9$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ngJAr",
      "text": "$2 x+3 y=-9$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "3J4SP",
      "text": "$2 x+3 y=-6$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Pm44P",
      "text": "$2 x+3 y=6$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & (2 y-5) \\frac{d y}{d x}=-3 \\\\ & (2 y-5) d y=-3 d x \\\\ & 2 \\cdot \\frac{y^2}{2}-5 y=-3 x+\\lambda\\end{aligned}$\n$\\because$ Curve passes through $(0,1)$\n$\\Rightarrow \\lambda=-4$\n$\\because$ Curve will be\n$\\left(y-\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^2=-3\\left(x-\\frac{3}{4}\\right)$\n$\\therefore$ Vertex of parabola will be $\\left(\\frac{3}{4}, \\frac{5}{2}\\right)$\n$\\because 2 x+3 y=9$",
    "image": null
  },
